The '''Koda Spur''' was a [[hyperspace route]] that ran from [[Koda Station]] of the [[Wazta sector]] eastward toward the [[Corellian Trade Spine]], terminating at the [[plant]] [[Lutrillia]] of the [[Greater Javin]] [[sector]]. Much of the route was in the Wazta sector, including the planets [[Thune]] and [[Lotho Minor]], with portions in both the [[Outer Rim Territories]] and [[Wild Space]].

==Description==
The Koda Spur was a [[hyperspace route]]<ref name="Scarif">{{EncyclopediaCite|Scarif and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> that ran from [[Koda Station]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Locations" /> eastward toward the [[Corellian Trade Spine]].<ref name="Scarif" /> Much of it passed through the [[Wazta sector]], ending in the [[Greater Javin]]'s [[Lutrillia system]].<ref name="Sectors" /> It passed through the [[Ryoone system]],<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> the [[Wild Space]] [[planet]]<ref name="Snare" /> [[Thune]], and the Outer Rim<ref name="Locations" /> planet<ref name="BMF 74">{{BuildFalconCite|74|Starship Fact File}}</ref> [[Lotho Minor]]<ref name="Locations" /> in [[Lotho Minor system]]<ref name="BMF 74" /> before terminating at<ref name="Locations" /> the planet<ref name="Traveler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref> [[Lutrillia]], which was linked to the Corellian Trade Spine by another route.<ref name="Locations" /> The planet [[Vassek]] in the [[Vassek system]] of the Wazta sector was far enough of the Koda Spur to ensure that it did not receive many visitors.<ref name="BMF 65">{{BuildFalconCite|65|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref>

==History==
In [[20 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' places the events of "[[Massacre]]" and "[[Revenge (episode)|Revenge]]" to [[20 BBY]]. The events of "[[Brothers (episode)|Brothers]]," during which a [[TR-TL3 Terrapin-class bulk tanker|''Terrapin''-class Bulk Tanker]] is hijacked, takes place between those two episodes according to {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}}, and so must also take place in 20 BBY.</ref> a [[TR-TL3 Terrapin-class bulk tanker|''Terrapin''-class Bulk Tanker]] was traveling between the [[planet]]s [[Stobar]] and [[Lotho Minor]] when it was hijacked near the Koda Spur by the [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] warrior [[Savage Opress]].<ref name="BMF 74">{{BuildFalconCite|74|Starship Fact File}}</ref> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], a repainted [[TIE series|TIE fighter]] was rumored to have been seen along the Koda Spur.<ref name="Shadow Fall">''[[Shadow Fall: An Alphabet Squadron Novel]]''</ref> Around [[5 ABY]],<ref name="5 ABY">{{ShadowFallDate}}</ref> while searching for activity of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[204th Imperial Fighter Wing]], the [[New Republic Intelligence]] [[agent]] [[Caern Adan]] and [[Lieutenant]] [[Yrica Quell]] reviewed the supposed sighting aboard the [[Acclamator-class transgalactic military assault ship|''Acclamator''-class transgalactic military assault ship]] ''[[Lodestar]]''.<ref name="Shadow Fall" />

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Starcruiserdate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]] to [[34 ABY]].</ref> the Koda Spur was included on a partial [[Star map|map]] of the [[galaxy]] displayed on screens on board [[Chandrila Star Line]]'s [[MPO-1400 Purgill-class star cruiser|Star Cruiser]] ''[[Halcyon]]'' while it traveled from the [[Core Worlds]]' [[Chandrila system]] to the Outer Rim Territories.<ref name="GS">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Koda Spur was first pictured on a map in "[[Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of Star Wars: The Force Awakens?|Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of ''Star Wars: The Force Awakens''?]]," a blog post on [[StarWars.com]] written by [[Mark Newbold]] and published on [[January 29]], [[2016]].<ref name="Where">{{SW|url=news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-star-wars-the-force-awakens|text=Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of ''Star Wars: The Force Awakens''?|int=Where in the Galaxy Are the Worlds of Star Wars: The Force Awakens?}}</ref> It was then first identified in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 65|sixty-fifth issue]] of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF 65" /> published around [[March 30]], 2016.<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|65}}</ref> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the [[Koda Spur/Legends|Koda Spur]] was first mentioned in the [[2009]] reference book ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'', which was written by [[Jason Fry]] and [[Daniel Wallace]].<ref name="Essential Atlas">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

